Tia (docs): Opening a small PR to add a "parsing rescue" section for tool-calling docs — covers nested arrays, missing optional fields, and the safe retry path. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1427
Sam (eng-runtime): Please note runtime behavior: on JSON parse failure we emit telemetry key `parse_shim_applied` and attempt a compact-envelope coercion. Call out route flags that signal parsed=true/false.
Jordan (devex): I'll add a streaming-safe example and a non-streaming retry example. Also will include a minimal test prompt that reproduces nested arrays: `Return actions as [[{"name":"x"}]]`.
Maria (sdk): Quick JS example (will port to Python):
```js
// parse-rescue.js
const r = await client.responses.create({ model: 'rw-open-7b', input: prompt });
try {
  const data = JSON.parse(r.output_text);
  // handle canonical shape
} catch (err) {
  // runtime applies coercion; client helper mirrors behavior
  const data = client.responses.parse_shim(r.output_text);
}
```
Chad (product): Add product note: Dedicated customers may see a small retry latency when the rescue path runs; recommend prefix caching for latency-sensitive routes.
deploy-bot: Preview for PR #1427: https://deploy-preview.redwood-inference.dev/docs/1427 (checks: lint ✓, link-checker ⚠ anchors)
Tia (docs): Plan: update PR with JS/Python snippets, streaming variant, telemetry note, product blurb, and fix stale anchors. Target: merge tomorrow AM.
